# Full pretraining baseline on v5e-64 — 10,000 steps, the sweep-v2 composed
# recipe. 10,000 x 524,288 = 5.24B tokens (~29 tok/param at ~181M params).
# ~40 min train at 0.23 s/step + val/ckpt overhead; RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5400
# leaves slack for compile and one preemption recovery.
#
# Recipe (docs/sweeps/v5e64-2026-07/report.md): LR 0.02, momentum warmup
# 0.85->0.95/300, emblr 0.3, unemb 0.002, cwd 0.2, clip 0.5, betas 0.8/0.95,
# warmup 1% (=100), ns_steps 5, mu_dtype f32, seed 0.
# Schedule: DECIDED by the preflight-schedule A/B (2026-07-22). composed+WSD-0.65
# = 3.3043 vs composed+cosine = 3.3250 at step 2446 (~13 sigma) -> WSD-0.65 wins.
# W&B: wsd x49i7l9j, cosine pbrbss3e. Flags applied below:
#   NANOGPT_LR_SCHEDULE=wsd NANOGPT_WSD_WARMDOWN_FRAC=0.65
#
# Self-heal: resume=auto + fixed WANDB_RUN_ID + GCS checkpoints every 100
# steps -> any relaunch (preemption reboot, coordinator restart) resumes
# from the latest checkpoint into the SAME W&B run (path verified
# 2026-07-20: write + all-16-host participation + resume 100->140).

TOTAL_TRAIN_STEPS=10000 PER_DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE=4 DATA_SHARDS=100 NANOGPT_VAL_MAX_BATCHES=25 NANOGPT_DEVICE_PEAK_FLOPS=197e12 RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5400 NANOGPT_EMBEDDING_LR=0.3 NANOGPT_UNEMBEDDING_LR=0.002 NANOGPT_CAUTIOUS_WD=0.2 NANOGPT_GRAD_CLIP_NORM=0.5 NANOGPT_LR_SCHEDULE=wsd NANOGPT_WSD_WARMDOWN_FRAC=0.65 NANOGPT_RESUME_FROM_STEP=auto SAVE_CKPT_DIR=gs://llm-architectures-eu/nanogptjax/checkpoints/v5e64-baseline-10k WANDB_RUN_GROUP=sweep2-v5e64 WANDB_JOB_TYPE=baseline WANDB_RUN_NAME=v5e64-baseline-10k WANDB_RUN_ID=v5e64-baseline-10k-r1
